From 6096ded65765154f5b5a8dd4e0a35b6384d051ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noah Cylich <noahcylich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:45:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] temporal-MoE CUDA: TEMPORAL_FUSED, one fused op per MoE layer
 on single-token steps

Off by default. The shared expert, the routed experts, the weighting and the sum over experts of one token
become one custom op that the CUDA backend runs as three launches; on the streamed path the op moves the
experts the routing op selected from the host-mapped pool into their slots inside those launches, so no
copy kernels, events or second stream are involved. The router, the softmax, the routing op and the gate-weight
ops stay ordinary graph nodes. Q4_0 experts with glm4moe's shapes only; other models keep the old path.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu |   7 +-
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/temporal.cu  | 194 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/temporal.cuh |   5 +
 src/llama-graph.cpp             |  34 ++++++
 src/llama-graph.h               |   4 +
 src/models/glm4-moe.cpp         |  12 ++
 6 files changed, 251 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

